<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">British conquest of Kano</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1903</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The British conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kano">Kano</a> took place in February 1903, when forces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-nigeria-protectorate">Protectorate of Northern Nigeria</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-lugard">Frederick Lugard</a> captured the city after a brief engagement. The defenders had no answer to British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maxim-gun">Maxim guns</a>. The fall of Kano, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphate</a>'s greatest commercial city, was quickly followed by the capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto</a> and the end of the Sokoto Caliphate's independence.</p></div>
